  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M. Mohammed vs Food Inspector on 8 February, 2016 Author: B.Sudheendra Kumar Bench: B.Sudheendra Kumar In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr. Justice B.Sudheendra Kumar Monday, The 8Th Day Of February 2016/19Th Magha, 1937 Crl.Rev.Pet.No. 1164 of 2013 () -------------------------------- Crl.A 688/2011 Of The Additional Sessions Court-Iii, Kozhikode St 181/2008 Of The Judicial Magistrate Of First Class - Ii, Perambra Revision Petitioner/Appellant/Accused: -------------------------------------- M. Mohammed, Aged 50 Years, S/O.Abdurahiman, Odakkunnampoyyil, Thalayad (Proprietor, News Bakery, Xi/173 Thalayad, Panangad Grama Panchayath By Adv. Sri.T.G.Rajendran Respondents/Complainant & State: ---------------------------- 1. Food Inspector Koyilandy- 673 305. 2. State Of Kerala Represented By Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam.",
    "facts": "The prosecution allegation can be briefly stated thus:- On 22.10.2007 at about 3.00 p.m., PW1, the Food Inspector purchased 600 gram of dried grape (raisins) from the first accused. The second accused was the distributor and the third accused was the manufacturer. After sampling as per rules, one sample was sent to the Public Analyst for analysis. After analysis, the Public Analyst submitted Ext.P13 report stating that the sample contained damaged raisins more than 2% and hence it did not conform to the standard prescribed for raisins as per the PFA Rules, 1955 and was therefore adulterated. Thereafter, on the request of the accused, the second sample was sent to the Central Food Laboratory for analysis. Ext.P21 certificate of the Central Food Laboratory would show that the sample did not conform to the standard prescribed for raisins under the PFA Rules and was therefore adulterated. It is further alleged that the revision petitioner did not have a valid licence under the PFA Rules to sell the food items. 4. Before the trial Court, PW1 to PW5 were examined and Exts.P1 to P28 were marked for the prosecution. DW1 to DW3 were examined and Exts.D1 to D3 were marked for the revision petitioner. M. Mohammed vs Food Inspector on 8 February, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/94604769/ 2",
